+# SDL GPU foundation library
+
+Shared, tested base for the SDL GPU renderer backends (wave 2). C++20, SDL3
+and the standard library only; no DS concepts. It sits underneath the
+game-facing backend interface (workstream 1b): a backend either issues draws
+as they happen or records them and issues them later in the frame; both end
+up in the same recorded order.
+
+Sources: `libraries/sim/src/gpu/*.cpp`, headers `include/simulator/gpu/*.hpp`,
+shaders `libraries/sim/src/gpu/shaders/`, toolchain
+`libraries/sim/tools/gpu_shaderc.py`, self-test
+`libraries/sim/tools/gpu_selftest.cpp`.
+
+Meson: `libraries/sim/src/gpu/meson.build` only defines `gpu_srcs` and
+`gpu_shader_headers`. The integrator enables the library with one line in
+`libraries/sim/src/meson.build`:
+
+```meson
+libsim_srcs += gpu_srcs
+```
+
+(plus the SDL3 dependency on `libsim_dependencies`).
+
+## Quick start
+
+```cpp
+#include <simulator/gpu/gpu.hpp>
+using namespace SIM::Gpu;
+
+Device device;
+device.Create();                              // windowless; SDL video is inited as needed
+Texture tex;
+tex.Create(device, TextureDesc::Rgba8(256, 192, "tex"));
+RenderTarget scene;
+scene.Create(device, 256 * 4, 192 * 4, SDL_GPU_TEXTUREFORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM, true, "scene");
+
+Frame *f = device.BeginFrame();
+f->UploadTexture(tex, pixels);                // runs in a copy pass before the draws that use it
+f->BeginPass(Phase::Scene3D, PassDesc::ColorDepth(scene.Color().Handle(), scene.Depth().Handle()));
+f->BindPipeline(device.Pipeline(key));        // PipelineKey: shaders, layout, blend, cull, depth, formats
+f->SetViewport(FullViewport(1024, 768));
+f->BindFragmentSampler(0, tex.Handle(), device.Sampler(SamplerKey::Nearest()));
+f->PushFragmentUniform(0, block);             // std140 block, copied at the call
+f->DrawStreamed(vertices, vertexCount, sizeof(Vertex));
+f->EndPass();
+f->BeginPass(Phase::Post, PassDesc::Color(target.Color().Handle()));
+// ... composite, post, overlay passes in phase order ...
+f->Present(target.Color().Handle(), target.Width(), target.Height());
+if (!f->End()) { /* already logged */ }
+std::vector<Uint8> px;
+device.ReadbackRGBA8(target.Color(), px);     // RGBA8, top row first
+```
+
+Every SDL GPU failure logs `SIM_GPU: <context>: <SDL_GetError()>` and fails
+loudly (false / nullptr / `Frame::End()` false). `SIM_GPU_DEBUG=1` enables
+SDL's debug mode, `SIM_GPU_DRIVER=vulkan|metal` forces a driver,
+`SIM_GPU_FATAL=1` aborts on the first failure.
+
+## Adding a shader
+
+1. Author Vulkan-flavoured GLSL (`#version 450`) in `shaders/`, e.g.
+   `post.frag`, following the resource-set rules below. A shader that uses
+   `#include` must enable the extension first:
+   ```glsl
+   #extension GL_GOOGLE_include_directive : enable
+   #include "sim_gpu.glsl"
+   ```
+2. Add its filename to `gpu_shaders` in `gpu/meson.build` (one line).
+3. `#include "post.frag.h"` in the backend and use
+   `SIM::Gpu::Shaders::post_frag`. `Device::Shader()` caches the compiled
+   shader; `Device::Pipeline(key)` caches the pipeline.
+
+`gpu_shaderc.py` (stdlib only) compiles the GLSL to SPIR-V with
+`glslangValidator`, reflects it with `spirv-cross`, cross-compiles to MSL,
+and emits a header with the SPIR-V bytes, the MSL source (macOS and iOS)
+and the resource counts `SDL_CreateGPUShader` needs. It fails with a clear
+error when a tool is missing, and rejects bindings that break SDL's rules,
+array resources, push constants, separate samplers/textures and uniform
+blocks over 32 KiB.
+
+## Resource binding rules (SPIR-V, enforced by gpu_shaderc.py)
+
+From `SDL_CreateGPUShader` in `SDL_gpu.h`:
+
+| Stage | Set for textures/storage | Set for uniform buffers |
+|---|---|---|
+| Vertex | 0: sampled textures, then storage textures, then storage buffers | 1 |
+| Fragment | 2: sampled textures, then storage textures, then storage buffers | 3 |
+
+Within each set, bindings are `0..n-1` with no gaps, in that order.
+Textures are combined image samplers (`sampler2D`, ...); SDL GPU has no
+separate samplers. Uniform blocks use `layout(std140, ...)`.
+
+### Metal binding rule (derived from SDL `SDL_gpu_metal.m`)
+
+SDL's Metal backend binds, per stage:
+
+| Resource | MSL attribute |
+|---|---|
+| Uniform buffer slot `i` | `[[buffer(i)]]` |
+| Storage buffer `j` | `[[buffer(num_uniform_buffers + j)]]` |
+| Sampled texture `k` | `[[texture(k)]]` and `[[sampler(k)]]` |
+| Storage texture `j` | `[[texture(num_samplers + j)]]` |
+| Vertex buffer slot `s` | `[[buffer(14 + s)]]` (via `[[stage_in]]`, never declared) |
+
+The SPIR-V bindings already equal these indices for uniform buffers,
+sampled textures and storage textures. Storage buffers do **not**: in
+SPIR-V a storage buffer sits at binding `num_samplers + num_storage_textures
++ j`, on Metal at `[[buffer(num_uniform_buffers + j)]]`. `gpu_shaderc.py`
+rewrites the storage-buffer `Binding` decorations in a private copy of the
+module before running `spirv-cross --msl-decoration-binding`, then checks
+every `[[buffer/texture/sampler(n)]]` in the generated entry point against
+the rule above. Shaders are compiled as **MSL 2.1** (`--msl-version 20100`):
+it covers everything these shaders use (including storage images/buffers
+and runtime arrays) while staying compatible back to macOS 10.14 / iOS
+12/13, far older than any target this project ships. Entry point is `main0`
+(SDL's default when the entrypoint is NULL; spirv-cross renames `main`).
+
+## Integer data: use a storage buffer, not a texture
+
+SDL GPU has no sampled-integer path: SDL forbids
+`SDL_GPU_TEXTUREUSAGE_SAMPLER` on integer formats, so there is no
+`texelFetch` / `usampler2D` path for VRAM, OAM or palette words. The
+tested path is a **storage buffer** (`Device::CreateBuffer` with
+`SDL_GPU_BUFFERUSAGE_GRAPHICS_STORAGE_READ`, bound with
+`Frame::BindFragmentStorageBuffer` / `BindVertexStorageBuffer`), declared in
+GLSL as
+
+```glsl
+layout(set = 2, binding = 0) readonly buffer Words { uint w[]; } words;
+// words.w[i] is the i-th 32-bit word; pack 16-bit words two per uint
+```
+
+and read as an array index. The self-test covers a 32-bit-word buffer and a
+packed-16-bit buffer end to end.
+
+Storage textures (`TextureDesc::R8Uint` / `R16Uint`, `uimage2D` +
+`imageLoad`, `Frame::BindFragmentStorageTexture`) work on Metal: the
+self-test's `integer-storage-texture` case (MSL only) reads exact pixels
+through them. But **they crash lavapipe (Mesa 26.1.1) on SDL 3.4.16** in
+every variant tried (R8/R16/R32_UINT, RGBA8, with and without
+`COMPUTE_STORAGE_WRITE`). The Vulkan backend in SDL 3.4.16 does not set
+`VK_IMAGE_USAGE_STORAGE_BIT` for `GRAPHICS_STORAGE_READ` textures (it only
+sets it for compute-write usages) while binding them as `STORAGE_IMAGE`
+descriptors — invalid Vulkan. So integer data that must work on both
+backends goes through storage buffers; storage textures are available for
+Metal-only or post-SDL-fix use, and the self-test skips their case on
+Vulkan so a lavapipe run stays green.
+
+MSL caution for storage buffers: spirv-cross emits an unsized `uint vals[]`
+as `uint vals[1]` in a `device` struct. Indexing past element 0 is pointer
+arithmetic on the `device` pointer and works in practice, but it is the one
+place where the MSL does not literally match the GLSL. The Mac self-test
+covers the SSBO path; if Metal ever rejects it, size the array in the shader
+to the data (e.g. `uint w[131072]` for 512 KiB of VRAM words).
+
+## Frame manager
+
+One command buffer per frame (`Device::BeginFrame` / `Frame::End`).
+Phases only order the frame: `Scene3D`, `Composite2D`, `Post`, `Overlay`;
+`BeginPass` must be called with non-decreasing phases, any number of
+passes may share a phase.
+
+* **Passes.** `BeginPass(phase, PassDesc)` / `EndPass()`. `PassDesc::Color`
+  / `ColorDepth` are the common cases. A depth target can be shared by
+  several passes in one frame (the 2D compositor's per-sprite draws use the
+  same depth texture as another phase): the later pass opens it with
+  `load = SDL_GPU_LOADOP_LOAD`, and the earlier pass must have opened it
+  with `store = SDL_GPU_STOREOP_STORE` (the default), or the depth is lost
+  on tile-based GPUs.
+* **Uploads.** `Frame::UploadTexture` / `UploadBuffer` run in a copy pass
+  before the draws that use them. An upload to a resource the open pass
+  has **not** referenced yet runs before the pass. An upload to a resource
+  the open pass **already** referenced splits the pass: the part recorded
+  so far is submitted, the upload runs, and the pass continues with LOAD
+  ops and the same bound state — earlier draws see the old data, later
+  draws the new data, exactly as with `glTexSubImage2D` between two GL
+  draws. `Frame::Stats().passSplits` counts the splits.
+* **Streaming vertices.** `StreamVertices` copies into the frame's vertex
+  stream; `BindStream(offset)` binds it; `DrawStreamed` does all three.
+  The stream buffer is kept across frames and cycled on first use per frame,
+  so frames in flight are not disturbed; it grows when a frame needs more.
+* **Uniforms.** `PushVertexUniform` / `PushFragmentUniform` (slot = GLSL
+  binding in set 1 / 3). Data is copied at the call, applies to later draws
+  in this frame, and does **not** carry over to the next frame. At most
+  32 KiB per push. A push recorded before a pass split still applies to the
+  continuation segment: SDL uniform state lives on the command buffer.
+* **Escape hatches.** `InPass(fn)` runs raw SDL calls inside the current
+  render pass (e.g. `ImGui_ImplSDLGPU3_RenderDrawData`); `OutsidePass(fn)`
+  runs between passes on the frame's command buffer (e.g.
+  `ImGui_ImplSDLGPU3_PrepareDrawData`, `SDL_BlitGPUTexture`). Resources an
+  `InPass` callback uses are not tracked for upload ordering.
+* **Present.** `Present(source, w, h, filter)` blits `source` onto the whole
+  swapchain texture at `End()`; a no-op when windowless. Keep `source` for
+  headless readback: the swapchain itself cannot be read. To render
+  straight into the swapchain, `AcquireSwapchain()` it and use it as a pass
+  target. SDL returns a **null swapchain** for a hidden/minimised window:
+  show the window before acquiring, or skip the draw when it is null.
+
+## Readback
+
+* **Synchronous:** `Device::ReadbackRGBA8(texture, out)` (RGBA8/BGRA8,
+  top-down, R/B swapped for BGRA) / `ReadbackRaw` (texels as stored). Waits
+  for the GPU. Call after `Frame::End()`.
+* **Per-frame (display capture):** `ReadbackRing(device, slots = 3)`.
+  `Request(texture, format, x, y, w, h)` after the frame that produced the
+  texture has ended records a download on its own command buffer and
+  returns a token; `Collect(token, out, wait)` hands the pixels back at a
+  fixed later point — typically the start of frame N+1, when the capture
+  must land in emulated VRAM before the game thread runs. With
+  `wait = false`, `Collect` returns false and leaves `out` untouched when
+  the download has not finished. The ring holds `slots` downloads in
+  flight; `Request` blocks only when the ring is full, waiting for the
+  oldest download, and a request whose result was never collected is
+  discarded when its slot is reused (`Collect` then returns false for that
+  token). The texture must stay alive until its result is collected.
+  Capture is rare enough that a synchronous wait on capture frames is the
+  fallback if a frame ever differs.
+
+## Pipelines and textures
+
+`PipelineKey` (shaders, vertex layout, primitive, cull, front face, depth
+test/compare/write, blend, colour write mask, colour/depth formats) keys
+`PipelineCache`: the same key returns the same pipeline, a different key
+another. Blend presets: `Opaque`, `Alpha` (GL
+`glBlendFunc(SRC_ALPHA, ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA)`, applied to alpha too),
+`Premultiplied`, `Additive`.
+
+`Texture` is an owning handle. `TextureDesc::ColorTarget` is a colour
+render target that can also be sampled and read back; `DepthTarget` uses
+the device's preferred depth format (`Device::DepthFormat()`: D24 where
+available, D32_FLOAT on Apple GPUs, else D16). `RenderTarget` is a colour
++ optional depth pair resized together (`Resize` returns whether the size
+changed; contents are undefined afterwards, clear on next use).
+
+`SamplerCache`: `SamplerKey::Nearest` / `Linear` with `Wrap::Repeat` /
+`Mirror` / `ClampToEdge`. Sampler state lives in the sampler object, not
+the texture. **GL_CLAMP_TO_BORDER has no SDL GPU equivalent** (Metal on iOS
+lacks border colours). For the DS "no repeat" case (transparent outside the
+texture), sample with `CLAMP_TO_EDGE` and, in the fragment shader, return
+the border colour when the coordinate is outside `[0, 1)`:
+
+```glsl
+if (any(lessThan(uv, vec2(0.0))) || any(greaterThanEqual(uv, vec2(1.0)))) c = vec4(0.0);
+```
+
+With NEAREST filtering this matches GL exactly; with LINEAR the edge
+texels blend toward the edge colour instead of the border colour.
+
+## Coordinate conventions
+
+| | OpenGL (current code) | SDL GPU (Vulkan and Metal alike) |
+|---|---|---|
+| NDC x, y | +Y up, (-1,-1) bottom-left | same: +Y up, (-1,-1) bottom-left |
+| NDC z / depth range | clip z in [-w, w], depth = z*0.5+0.5 | clip z in [0, w], depth = z |
+| Viewport / scissor | origin bottom-left, +Y up | origin top-left, +Y down |
+| Framebuffer memory | row 0 = bottom row (`glReadPixels` returns bottom-up, code flips it) | row 0 = top row (downloads are top-down, no flip needed) |
+| Texture upload | row 0 of the data -> t = 0 | row 0 of the data -> v = 0 |
+| Texture sampling | t = 0 reads data row 0 | v = 0 reads data row 0 |
+| Render-to-texture | NDC +Y lands in the LAST row, so a render target is sampled with t = 1 at its visual top | NDC +Y lands in row 0, so a render target is sampled with v = 0 at its visual top |
+| Front face | `glFrontFace(GL_CW / GL_CCW)`, judged on the image as it appears on screen | `SDL_GPU_FRONTFACE_CLOCKWISE / _COUNTER_CLOCKWISE`, judged the same way (SDL compensates for Vulkan's flipped NDC) |
+| Cull | `GL_FRONT` / `GL_BACK` / `GL_FRONT_AND_BACK` | FRONT / BACK only: skip the draw for FRONT_AND_BACK |
+
+What a port from GL has to change, and nothing else (helpers in
+`coords.hpp`, shader helpers in `shaders/sim_gpu.glsl`):
+
+1. **Depth:** a vertex shader that outputs GL clip-space z must remap it,
+   or every z < 0 is clipped:
+   `gl_Position = SIM_GL_TO_GPU_DEPTH(gl_Position)` i.e.
+   `gl_Position.z = (gl_Position.z + gl_Position.w) * 0.5`. Depth compares
+   (LESS, EQUAL, ...) keep working because the remap is monotonic and exact
+   for the same input. Feed the original z to anything else that reads it
+   (e.g. fog).
+2. **Viewport and scissor:** `y_gpu = targetHeight - y_gl - height`
+   (`GlViewport` / `GlScissor`).
+3. **Sampling a texture that was RENDERED** (not uploaded) with GL-style
+   coordinates: use `v_gpu = 1 - v_gl` (`SIM_RT_UV` in `sim_gpu.glsl`, or
+   flip the quad's texture coordinates). CPU-uploaded textures need no
+   change.
+4. **Readback:** drop the bottom-up row flip the GL code does after
+   `glReadPixels`.
+5. **`gl_FragCoord.y`** counts from the top in SDL GPU and from the bottom
+   in GL: `y_gl = targetHeight - gl_FragCoord.y` (only matters for shaders
+   that use `gl_FragCoord.y`).
+
+## Exact depth equality
+
+The stat-change effect draws the arrow pattern with the DS **equal** depth
+test over the battler's mesh, vertex for vertex. Two draws must produce
+bitwise-identical depth, which requires the vertex shaders to compute
+identical `gl_Position` values — the compiler may optimise algebraically
+identical expressions differently, so declare
+
+```glsl
+invariant gl_Position;
+```
+
+in every vertex shader that feeds an EQUAL (or otherwise
+cross-draw-compared) depth test, and keep the position math identical in
+spirit across those shaders. The self-test's `invariant-depth-equal` case
+draws the same mesh twice through two vertex shaders with algebraically
+identical but textually different position math (`pos` vs
+`pos.x * 2.0 * 0.5`), the second with depth compare EQUAL, and checks every
+covered pixel passes. Use `invariant` on the 3D vertex shader and on the
+effect shader in wave 2; `precise` on individual expressions is the
+finer-grained alternative.
+
+## What OpenGL 4.1 offered that SDL GPU does not
+
+* **Clamp-to-border** — see the shader-side test above.
+* **`glReadPixels` of the default framebuffer** — read back an offscreen
+  target instead; the swapchain cannot be read.
+* **Sampler state on textures** — sampler objects bound next to each
+  texture at draw time.
+* **Uniforms that persist between draws** — uniform slots live on the
+  command buffer; push again every frame (a background shader's uniforms
+  in the CPU 2D path, for example, are pushed per frame).
+* **Global state / default framebuffer** — draws happen in explicit render
+  passes on explicit targets; pipeline objects bake cull/depth/blend.
+* **Geometry shaders** — not in SDL GPU; do not design for them (also
+  absent on Metal / mobile GPUs).
+* **Front-and-back culling** — SDL GPU pipelines have a single cull mode:
+  skip the draw for `FRONT_AND_BACK`.
+* **Stencil and depth bias** — SDL GPU does expose them (front/back stencil
+  ops and masks in the pipeline, stencil reference set dynamically per
+  pass; depth bias in the rasterizer state), but `PipelineKey` does not
+  cover them yet. If wave 2 needs either, extend `PipelineKey`. The
+  simulator's current GL renderer does not use stencil; depth-stencil
+  combined formats (`D24_UNORM_S8_UINT`) exist if one is ever needed.
+* **Sampled integer textures** — see "Integer data" above.
+
+## Self-test
+
+```sh
+# Devserver (SDL 3.4.16 in /data/repos/dp-wt/sdl3-deps/prefix):
+source tools/sdl_gpu_migration/env_devserver.sh
+export VK_ICD_FILENAMES=/usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/lvp_icd.x86_64.json
+meson setup build libraries/sim/tools/gpu_selftest && ninja -C build
+./build/gpu_selftest                    # windowless, no DISPLAY, lavapipe
+xvfb-run -a ./build/gpu_selftest --windowed   # windowed path, real swapchain
+SIM_GPU_DEBUG=1 ./build/gpu_selftest    # SDL's own validation
+```
+
+One PASS/FAIL line per case; exit non-zero on any mismatch. Cases:
+windowless device; textured, vertex-coloured, depth-tested draw with
+readback against expected pixels including an orientation check (an
+asymmetric pattern must come back upright and unmirrored); alpha blending;
+cull and depth-compare permutations through the pipeline cache; integer
+data through storage buffers (32-bit words and packed 16-bit words);
+a uniform block with an int array and a float array (std140 end to end;
+the 3D shader has two 32-float fog tables); sub-region texture updates;
+upload-queue ordering (a mid-pass upload splits the pass); many small draws
+in one frame; render-target resize; a depth target shared by two passes in
+one frame; exact depth equality with `invariant gl_Position`; ring
+readback (frame N's download collected after later frames ran, plus ring
+wrap discarding an uncollected request); and, with `--windowed`, a draw
+into the swapchain plus present and readback of the present target.
+
+### Mac self-test
+
+Homebrew on the Mac is not writable by agents, so `glslang` / `spirv-cross`
+are **not** installed there. The shader blobs (SPIR-V + MSL + C arrays)
+are generated on the devserver and the generated sources copied to the Mac
+for the self-test build — the self-test's meson build detects the missing
+tools and uses pre-generated headers from the build directory instead.
+Homebrew SDL3 3.4.16 is installed. The windowed case shows the window on
+non-Apple platforms (SDL returns a null swapchain for hidden windows); on
+Apple the window stays hidden per the headless-only Mac rule and the
+swapchain draw is skipped when it comes back null.
+
+## Public API (one line per function)
+
+`Device`: `Create` (windowless device, optional debug/driver/env) /
+`Destroy` / `AttachWindow` / `DetachWindow` / `SetVsync` (runtime, VSYNC /
+MAILBOX / IMMEDIATE) / `SwapchainFormat` / `Shader` (cached per blob) /
+`Pipeline` (via `Pipelines().Get`) / `Sampler` (via `Samplers().Get`) /
+`BeginFrame` / `CurrentFrame` / `UploadTexture` (whole / sub-region, queues
+outside a frame) / `UploadBuffer` / `FlushUploads` / `CreateBuffer` /
+`ReadbackRGBA8` (sync) / `ReadbackRaw` (sync) / `WaitIdle` / `Failed` /
+`ClearFailed` / `ReportFailure` / `DriverName` / `ShaderFormat` /
+`DepthFormat` / `SupportsTexture`.
+
+`Frame`: `BeginPass` / `EndPass` / `BindPipeline` / `SetViewport` /
+`SetScissor` / `SetBlendConstants` / `BindVertexBuffer` /
+`BindIndexBuffer` / `BindVertexSampler` / `BindFragmentSampler` /
+`BindVertexStorageTexture` / `BindFragmentStorageTexture` /
+`BindVertexStorageBuffer` / `BindFragmentStorageBuffer` / `Draw` /
+`DrawIndexed` / `StreamVertices` / `BindStream` / `DrawStreamed` /
+`PushVertexUniform` / `PushFragmentUniform` / `InPass` / `OutsidePass` /
+`UploadTexture` (whole / sub-region) / `UploadBuffer` /
+`AcquireSwapchain` / `Present` / `End` / `Stats` / `Index` / `Failed`.
+
+`PipelineCache`: `Get` (creates on first use) / `Size` / `Clear`.
+`SamplerCache`: `Get` / `Clear`.
+`Texture`: `Create` / `Resize` / `Release` / `Handle` / `Desc` / `Width` /
+`Height` / `Format`. `RenderTarget`: `Create` / `Resize` / `Release` /
+`Color` / `Depth` / `HasDepth`.
+`ReadbackRing`: `Request` / `Collect` / `HasOutstanding` / `Slots`.
+Coords: `GlViewport` / `GlScissor` / `FullViewport` /
+`GlNdcDepthToGpu` / `GlRenderTargetV` / `GlFrontFace`.
+std140: `Std140Array<T, N>` (+ `Assign`) / `Std140Element` /
+`Std140Vec4` / `Std140IVec4` / `Std140Vec2` / `Std140IVec2`.
+
+## Open risks
+
+* **Metal is still the likeliest silent failure** (MSL generation, binding
+  mapping, SSBO unsized arrays, storage textures). The Mac self-test retires
+  most of it; run it before wave 2 leans on MSL.
+* **Storage textures work on Metal, crash lavapipe** (the SDL Vulkan
+  STORAGE_BIT bug above is upstream). Integer data that must work on both
+  backends goes through storage buffers.
+* **Pixel-exactness of 3D between rasterisers** — thresholds per scenario,
+  as in the plan; the foundation makes no exactness claim beyond the
+  self-test's cases.
+* **Capture readback latency vs determinism** — the ring defers the stall
+  by a frame; if any frame differs, fall back to a synchronous wait on
+  capture frames only.
+* **Frames in flight vs `cycle`:** a pass that overwrites a target with
+  `load != LOAD` and `cycle = true` gets fresh storage; a pass that loads
+  a target another frame in flight still reads must not cycle it. The
+  backend owns that choice per target.
+* **ImGui:** the vendored ImGui may predate `imgui_impl_sdlgpu3`; wave 2c
+  decides the smallest update. The `InPass` / `OutsidePass` escape hatches
+  are the integration points.
